1. Fundamental Structural Hierarchy & Package Architecture
The architecture spans from foundational biological cellular levels up to global ecosystems, structured via
modular Java package hierarchies:
Cells: Basic structural/functional units (e.g., neurons, red blood cells, specialized tissue grids).
Tissues: Groups of similar cells working together (e.g., neural tissue grids with simulated cell states like 
HEALTHY\_NEURAL, TUMOR\_ACTIVE, TUMOR\_NECROTIC, and THERAPY\_APPLIED).
Organs & Organ Systems: Coordinated anatomical structures managing physiological workloads across
11 standardized subsystems.
Organism Tier: Complete integrated individual entities containing all 11 systems.
Ecological Tiers: Populations, communities, ecosystems, biomes, and biosphere simulation layers.
